{% comment %}
  Education & Guides - the friendly Learn page.

  Same guides and the same copy as 'learn-hub', re-dressed: a picture at the top
  of each card, soft rounded corners on a cream field, a pill in place of the
  bare number, sentence-case titles, a nudging arrow, and a closing panel that
  offers a person once the reading is done.

  Where a card's picture comes from, in order:
    1. "Image" on the block, chosen in the theme editor;
    2. "Image file name" on the block, a file under assets/ (the shipped guides
       reuse the mega menu's pictures, e.g. featured-diamonds-education.jpg);
    3. nothing - the card keeps its tint and reads as type, and a file name that
       does not resolve hides the picture rather than leaving a broken frame.

  Every look is a setting: colours, type sizes, corner radius, columns, image
  ratio and the closing panel's button all come from the schema below and are
  written out as custom properties. assets/education-guides.css holds the shape.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'education-guides.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign stts = section.settings
  assign topics = section.blocks
  assign columns = stts.columns | default: 3

  comment
    A tablet never shows more than two across, and never more than the desktop
    count, so a single-column choice stays single all the way up.
  endcomment
  assign columns_tablet = 2
  if columns < 2
    assign columns_tablet = columns
  endif

  comment
    An arbitrary file under assets/ has no size the theme can know, so the img
    declares the frame's own proportions instead: the ratio chosen in the editor
    at a nominal 900px wide. .eg-card__media crops to the same ratio, so the
    declared size is what the picture actually occupies and nothing shifts while
    it loads. A picture chosen with the image picker carries its real size via
    image_tag and skips all of this.
  endcomment
  assign ratio_parts = stts.image_ratio | split: '/'
  assign ratio_w = ratio_parts[0] | strip | times: 1
  assign ratio_h = ratio_parts[1] | strip | times: 1
  if ratio_w < 1
    assign ratio_w = 1
  endif
  if ratio_h < 1
    assign ratio_h = 1
  endif
  assign asset_width = 900
  assign asset_height = asset_width | times: ratio_h | divided_by: ratio_w
-%}

{%- style -%}
  #education-guides-{{ section.id }} {
    --eg-columns-desktop: {{ columns }};
    --eg-columns-tablet: {{ columns_tablet }};
    --eg-ink: {{ stts.text_color }};
    --eg-muted: {{ stts.muted_text_color }};
    --eg-card-bg: {{ stts.card_background }};
    --eg-card-border: {{ stts.card_border_color }};
    --eg-accent: {{ stts.accent_color }};
    --eg-radius: {{ stts.card_radius }}px;
    --eg-gap: {{ stts.card_gap | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-ratio: {{ stts.image_ratio }};
    --eg-heading-size: {{ stts.heading_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-body-size: {{ stts.body_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-card-title-size: {{ stts.card_title_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-card-text-size: {{ stts.card_text_size | divided_by: 10.0 }}rem;
    --eg-cta-bg: {{ stts.cta_background }};
    --eg-cta-ink: {{ stts.cta_text_color }};
    --eg-btn-bg: {{ stts.cta_button_background }};
    --eg-btn-ink: {{ stts.cta_button_text_color }};
    background: {{ stts.background }};
    color: {{ stts.text_color }};
    padding-block: {{ stts.padding_top }}px {{ stts.padding_bottom }}px;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<section
  id="education-guides-{{ section.id }}"
  class="education-guides color-{{ stts.color_scheme }}"
>
  <div class="eg-shell">
    <div class="eg-intro">
      {%- if stts.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="eg-eyebrow">{{ stts.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if stts.heading != blank -%}
        <h1 class="eg-heading">{{ stts.heading | escape }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if stts.description != blank -%}
        <div class="eg-description rte">{{ stts.description }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if topics.size == 0 -%}
      <p class="eg-empty">Add a guide to this section in the theme editor.</p>
    {%- else -%}
      <ul class="eg-grid" role="list">
        {%- for block in topics -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign title = block.settings.title
            if title == blank
              continue
            endif

            assign badge = block.settings.badge
            if badge == blank
              assign badge = forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2
            endif

            assign label = block.settings.link_label | default: 'Learn more'
            assign has_link = false
            if block.settings.link != blank
              assign has_link = true
            endif

            assign picture = block.settings.image
            assign picture_asset = blank
            if picture == blank
              assign picture_asset = block.settings.image_asset | strip
            endif

            comment
              Spelt out as nested conditions rather than one `and`/`or` line,
              because Liquid has no parentheses and reads such a line right to left.
            endcomment
            assign has_media = false
            if stts.show_images
              if picture != blank or picture_asset != blank
                assign has_media = true
              endif
            endif
          -%}

          <li class="eg-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- if has_link -%}
              <a class="eg-card__link eden-action-host" href="{{ block.settings.link }}">
            {%- else -%}
              <div class="eg-card__link">
            {%- endif -%}

              {%- if has_media -%}
                <div class="eg-card__media">
                  {%- if picture != blank -%}
                    {{
                      picture
                      | image_url: width: 900
                      | image_tag:
                        loading: 'lazy',
                        sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 33vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw',
                        alt: title
                    }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      A file under assets/, resized by the CDN. No intrinsic size is
                      known for an arbitrary file, so the ratio on .eg-card__media
                      holds the space and the script below hides a 404.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <img
                      src="{{ picture_asset | asset_img_url: '900x' }}"
                      srcset="
                        {{ picture_asset | asset_img_url: '450x' }} 450w,
                        {{ picture_asset | asset_img_url: '700x' }} 700w,
                        {{ picture_asset | asset_img_url: '900x' }} 900w
                      "
                      sizes="(min-width: 990px) 33vw, (min-width: 750px) 50vw, 100vw"
                      alt="{{ title | escape }}"
                      width="{{ asset_width }}"
                      height="{{ asset_height }}"
                      loading="lazy"
                      data-eg-asset
                    >
                  {%- endif -%}

                  {%- if stts.show_numbers -%}
                    <span class="eg-card__badge">{{ badge | escape }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}

              <div class="eg-card__body">
                {%- if stts.show_numbers and has_media == false -%}
                  <span class="eg-card__badge">{{ badge | escape }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}

                <h2 class="eg-card__title">{{ title | escape }}</h2>

                {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
                  <p class="eg-card__text">{{ block.settings.text | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if has_link -%}
                  <span class="eg-card__action">
                    {{- label | escape -}}
                    <span class="eg-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

            {%- if has_link -%}
              </a>
            {%- else -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if stts.show_cta and stts.cta_heading != blank -%}
      <div class="eg-cta">
        <div class="eg-cta__copy">
          <p class="eg-cta__heading">{{ stts.cta_heading | escape }}</p>
          {%- if stts.cta_text != blank -%}
            <div class="eg-cta__text rte">{{ stts.cta_text }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if stts.cta_button_label != blank and stts.cta_button_link != blank -%}
          <a class="eg-cta__button eden-action eden-action--solid" href="{{ stts.cta_button_link }}">
            {{- stts.cta_button_label | escape -}}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  A card can name a file under assets/ that the shop has not uploaded yet. Rather
  than leave a broken frame, the picture is dropped and the card carries on as
  type - the same card the "Show pictures" switch produces.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (() => {
    const root = document.getElementById('education-guides-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root) return;
    root.querySelectorAll('img[data-eg-asset]').forEach((img) => {
      img.addEventListener('error', () => img.closest('.eg-card__media')?.remove());
    });
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Education & guides",
  "class": "section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "Education & guides"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Everything you need to know, in plain language"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Introduction",
      "default": "<p>There is a lot to take in when you are choosing fine diamond and gemstone jewellery, from an engagement ring to a pair of everyday earrings. Explore the guides below to learn about diamonds and gemstones, caring for your jewellery, finding your ring size and more.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns",
      "label": "Guides across on desktop",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3,
      "info": "A tablet shows at most two, and a phone one."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_gap",
      "label": "Space between cards",
      "min": 8,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_radius",
      "label": "Corner rounding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 36,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_images",
      "label": "Show pictures",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_ratio",
      "label": "Picture shape",
      "options": [
        { "value": "4 / 3", "label": "Landscape (4:3)" },
        { "value": "3 / 2", "label": "Landscape (3:2)" },
        { "value": "1 / 1", "label": "Square" },
        { "value": "4 / 5", "label": "Portrait (4:5)" },
        { "value": "16 / 9", "label": "Wide (16:9)" }
      ],
      "default": "1 / 1",
      "info": "The guide pictures are portrait, so a square frame keeps more of each one than a landscape crop."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_numbers",
      "label": "Show the pill on each card",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Numbers the guides unless a card sets its own pill text."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Type sizes"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "label": "Heading size",
      "min": 24,
      "max": 64,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 44
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "body_size",
      "label": "Introduction size",
      "min": 13,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 17
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_title_size",
      "label": "Card title size",
      "min": 14,
      "max": 32,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 21
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "card_text_size",
      "label": "Card text size",
      "min": 12,
      "max": 22,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 15
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colours"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:settings.color_scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "Section background",
      "default": "#fdf9f7"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Headings and titles",
      "default": "#171714"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "muted_text_color",
      "label": "Body text",
      "default": "#5c5a55"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "card_background",
      "label": "Card background",
      "default": "#ffffff"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "card_border_color",
      "label": "Card border",
      "default": "#ebe4df"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Pills and picture tint",
      "default": "#ead9d1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Closing panel"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_cta",
      "label": "Show the closing panel",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Still deciding? Talk it through with us."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "cta_text",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<p>Our team can walk you through stones, settings and sizing, and help you choose with confidence.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_button_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "Get in touch"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_button_link",
      "label": "Button link"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "cta_background",
      "label": "Panel background",
      "default": "#ead9d1"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "cta_text_color",
      "label": "Panel text",
      "default": "#171714"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "cta_button_background",
      "label": "Button background",
      "default": "#171714"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "cta_button_text_color",
      "label": "Button text",
      "default": "#ffffff"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 56
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 80
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "topic",
      "name": "Guide",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Description"
        },
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Image"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "image_asset",
          "label": "Image file name",
          "info": "A file under assets/, e.g. featured-diamonds-education.jpg. Used only when no image is chosen above, and ignored if the file is missing."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "badge",
          "label": "Pill text",
          "info": "Leave empty to number the guide."
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "link",
          "label": "Link",
          "info": "Leave empty while the guide is still being written and the card shows as plain text."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "link_label",
          "label": "Link text",
          "default": "Learn more"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Education & guides",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The 4 C's",
            "text": "Cut, colour, clarity and carat weight are what decide a diamond's beauty and its price. Of the four, cut does the most for sparkle.",
            "image_asset": "featured-diamonds-education.jpg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "About lab-grown diamonds",
            "text": "Grown rather than mined, and identical to a mined diamond in chemistry, structure and brilliance - at roughly 40% less.",
            "image_asset": "lifestyle-princess-ring.jpg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Lab-grown gemstones",
            "text": "Real sapphires, rubies and emeralds with the same properties as their mined counterparts, in colours that are hard to find in nature.",
            "image_asset": "featured-diamonds-gemstones.jpg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Stone comparison",
            "text": "Where a lab-grown diamond sits next to a simulant such as cubic zirconia or moissanite, and how to tell one from the other.",
            "image_asset": "lifestyle-emerald-earring.jpg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Find your ring size",
            "text": "A printable ring sizer, an international conversion chart, and what to do when you are buying a surprise.",
            "image_asset": "featured-diamonds-sizing.jpg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Find the right metal",
            "text": "Platinum, and 14K or 18K white, yellow and rose gold - how each wears day to day and which suits which stone.",
            "image_asset": "menu-tile-plain-metal-wedding-bands.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Jewellery care & cleaning",
            "text": "How to clean your pieces at home, when to have them checked, and the habits that keep a setting secure for years.",
            "image_asset": "featured-diamonds-care.jpg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "topic",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Glossary of jewellery terms",
            "text": "Bezel, pave, culet, girdle - the words you will meet while you shop, in plain language.",
            "image_asset": "lifestyle-round-necklace.jpg"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
